/// Generate text responses from text prompts. This endpoint supports both streaming and non-streaming responses for supported text models.
///
/// [model] The model ID of the model you want to use. Get the model ID using
///   `/v1/models` or on the available models page.
/// [input] The prompt or input content you want the model to respond to. Can be
///   a simple text string or an array of message objects for conversation
///   context.
/// [maxOutputTokens] The maximum number of tokens to generate in the response.
/// [temperature] A value between 0.0 and 2.0 to control randomness and
///   creativity. Lower values like 0.2 make the output more focused and
///   deterministic, while higher values like 0.8 make it more random.
/// [stream] Set to true to stream partial responses as Server-Sent Events.
/// [instructions] System-level instructions for the model. This sets the
///   behavior and context for the response generation.
/// [topP] An alternative to sampling with temperature, called nucleus sampling,
///   where the model considers the results of the tokens with top_p probability
///   mass.
/// [streamOptions] Options for streaming response. Only set this when you set
///   stream to true.
/// [tools] A list of tools the model may call.
